    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), derived from the owner's own fields.\n\n**Algorithm:** start at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure).\n\n### Files changed\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` (string, GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE) schema property with `membershipLevel` (int32, min 1, max 3, `readOnly`) and updated its description. The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, so the response now exposes `membershipLevel` instead of `membershipTier`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` MapStruct expression with a `membershipLevel` one:\n   ```java\n   Math.min(3, 1 + (email present ? 1 : 0) + (namesakeCount == 0 ? 1 : 0))\n   ```\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 The create audit line now records `membershipLevel` instead of the tier. I moved the `toOwnerDto` mapping just above the audit call so the derived level is available to log.\n\n### Notes\n- The membership value was (and remains) a derived field computed by the mapper from stored fields (`email`, `namesakeCount`), so a create-then-GET returns the same value \u2014 matching the \"assigned on creation\" semantics without adding a persisted column.\n- The existing audit line did not literally record the old tier string, but per the spec (\"anything that recorded the tier \u2026 must record the level instead\"), the create audit line now carries `membershipLevel`.\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` (unique name + email \u2192 1 +email +namesake0, capped 3 = **3**) passes, and the full suite is green.",
